Model scripts (run from the project root, results go to Results/Analysis)

Composition model (Julia, functions in FinalModel_functions.jl and CompositionModel_functions.jl):
- Main_base.jl: base scenario (aggregated_trips.csv)
- Main_GGV.jl: GGV scenario (aggregated_trips_merged_GGV.csv), the GGV rules can be switched on one by one
- Main_compareScenarios.jl, Main_Mtrains.jl, Main_parking.jl: scenario comparisons (several runs)

Unit assignment (post-solution step):
- Main_assignUnits.py: assigns physical units (e.g. ICA_12) to the compositions of a result and checks the
  assignment against the model (functions in AssignUnits_functions.py). By default it takes the newest result.
  It follows the UnitFlows file that write_results writes with every result.
- Export_unitFlows.jl <scenario> <timestamp>: writes the UnitFlows file for results solved before it existed.

Diagrams of a result: Visualization/Main_diagrams.py

Archive: old models with their own model code (simple model, unit preservation, old GGV model) and an old
test script. They are not maintained and their paths assume they are in Models/.
